    "created_at": "2021-09-22T16:41:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-22T16:41:11Z",
    "body": "I think we have a more fundamental question here, which I am encouraging you to take up with TC39: are JavaScript exception messages supposed to be localized? Are they supposed to be user-facing or developer-facing? My strong intuition is that they are developer-facing and not supposed to be localized, but instead the same across all locales to aid searchability etc.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/webidl/issues/comments/925099125/reactions",
